<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds slid lower on Tuesday in the wake of German Bund losses, as the mark was once again beaten lower against the dollar, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said bonos would remain tied to developments in Bunds and the mark in the short-term. German unemployment data for July scheduled to be released at 0800 GMT on Wednesday will be closely watched, they added.</p>
<p>&quot;We've seen the peseta/mark break through 84.50 today and the market is nervous with the mark weakening so much and the dollar steaming ahead,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
</text>
